{
  "comment": "The human muscle template of the Flicker Void tools (meatbag_factory/anatomy.py), for UE4 and UE5 Mannequin skeletons. Every muscle is written for the left side and mirrored. A muscle is a list of strands [origin, insertion]: one for a simple muscle, several for a fan (pectoral, trapezius, quadriceps). Hooks are extra points a strand also bends with (gluteus). An attachment sits 'along' its bone (0 at the joint, 1 at the next joint of the chain), and is pushed toward the skin in 'direction' = [front, left, up] of the body, keeping 'depth' (default 0.4) of the way back from the skin. width and thickness scale the room under the skin at the belly. drives = corrective roles (Rig/CorrectiveRoles.json) the muscle moves, with weights. Names must stay stable: projects store them.",
